{
  "summary": "Configure Guix to build Linux x86_64 and aarch64 non-GUI release binaries (bitcoind and CLI tools) as static position-independent executables (-static-pie) using glibc 2.44. Apply patches to glibc to eliminate non-deterministic /gnu/store paths and disable NSS module runtime dlopening. Adjust Guix symbol-check and security-check verification scripts to support and validate static ELF binaries.",
  "problem": "Linux release binaries dynamically link against glibc and the system dynamic linker, preventing them from running on non-glibc distributions like Alpine Linux or on systems with glibc versions older than the build environment. Dynamic linking also complicates security mitigations such as aarch64 pointer authentication (#19075).",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: shows `file bitcoind` reporting `ELF 64-bit LSB pie executable ... static-pie linked` and `ldd` reporting `statically linked` across multiple distributions including Alpine, CentOS, Debian, and NixOS.",
    "doc/release-notes-25573.md: notes release binaries for x86_64 and aarch64 Linux 'can now be run on non-glibc based systems, as well as on systems than ship with older glibcs' but warns that 'name resolution through dynamic nss modules is not possible' (e.g., mDNS, LDAP, SSSD)."
  ],
