  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches Guix build scripts, package definitions, glibc source patches (to remove store paths and dlopen behavior), and post-build ELF validation scripts.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased onto recent build system changes with no major structural alterations.",
  "card": "Configures Guix to build official Linux x86_64 and aarch64 release binaries (excluding bitcoin-qt) as static position-independent executables (-static-pie) using glibc 2.44. This eliminates dynamic linker dependencies, allowing bitcoind and utilities to run on musl-based distributions like Alpine Linux and on older Linux installations, while enabling aarch64 pointer authentication (#19075). Statically compiling glibc means dynamic NSS modules (such as mDNS, LDAP, or SSSD) will no longer function for name resolution. Post-build symbol and security check scripts are updated to validate static ELF binaries.",
